<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eric Hobsbawm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/2012">2012</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Eric John Ernest Hobsbawm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eric Hobsbawm was a British historian of the rise of industrial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitalism">capitalism</a>, socialism and nationalism and a life-long Marxist. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, he grew up in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> and moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1933; at King's College, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambridge">Cambridge</a>, he joined the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>. He taught at Birkbeck College, University of London, from 1947 and was its president from 2002 until his death. His best-known works are his books on the long 19th century, among them The Age of Revolution: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> 1789–1848, The Age of Capital and The Age of Empire, The Age of Extremes on the short 20th century, and an edited volume that introduced the idea of invented traditions.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Where no organisation existed, protest took the form of bread riots, petitions and what the historian <b>Eric Hobsbawm</b> called “collective bargaining by riot”.</blockquote><a href="/movement/labour-movement">Labour movement · Background</a></li><li><blockquote>The historian Malcolm I. Thomis argued that the attacks implied no hostility to machinery as such, and <b>Eric Hobsbawm</b> called them “collective bargaining by riot”.</blockquote><a href="/movement/luddites">Luddites · Aims</a></li></ul></section>
